    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on favorable matchups today, with **Kyle Tucker** (82.87) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) anchoring the lineup. **Kyle Tucker** is our premier play; he draws a soft matchup against Lowder, and the combination of an elevated SP xERA of 4.82 and a solid park factor positions him for elite production. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from an excellent SP skill matchup (+19%) against Ober. While **Heliot Ramos** (66.28) carries a lower base, his ability to exploit Ober\u2019s slow delivery\u2014which elevates his stolen base upside\u2014makes him a critical secondary contributor as we hunt for scarcity in the SB category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was leaving **Coby Mayo** (52.30) on the bench. He hovered near the starting threshold throughout the morning, and his favorable platoon edge against Manaea provided a strong case for inclusion. Ultimately, the projection favored the higher baseline efficiency of our corner infield starters, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Miguel Vargas**. **Miguel Vargas** in particular earned his spot with a 55.12 score, buoyed by wind blowing out and a productive batting order slot. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler** failed to meet our 40.0 \"Zebras Floor\" due to tough pitching matchups and, in the case of **Nasim Nunez**, a bottom-of-the-order placement that severely limits his run-production potential.\n\nWe are monitoring the risk profile of **Gunnar Henderson** (49.27) closely. While he remains a core part of our strategy, his matchup against Manaea is dampened by a -15% platoon penalty and the opposing pitcher's elite ability to hold runners (63% SB prevention), which creates a significant drag on his peripheral value. We are currently operating without **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains sidelined on the IL, but with the rest of the squad healthy and clear of major weather warnings, we are positioned to maintain our efficiency targets. We will keep a close watch on **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** to ensure they handle their respective right-handed matchups effectively to keep our 5x5 pace steady.",
